-- title:
--   Integral cusp-regular level-M' functions lie in the j_ℓ-chart algebra
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, an integer $M'\ne 0$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in whose nonunits $q$ lies. Let $R_0$ be a constant reduction datum for $A$ on the field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$, the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((\mathsf q))$ generated over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ by the coefficientwise images of the $\mathbb Q$-subfield generated by the series $\mathsf q\mapsto \mathsf q^{d}$ transports of $j$ for $d\mid M'$, with values in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}$ of the residue field of $A$; thus $R_0$ consists of a valuation subring `R₀.integers`, a surjective residue map onto that field with kernel the maximal ideal, a map on places preserving degrees, compatibility with $A$ and with divisor pushforward, and the scaling property. Assume in addition ($hR_0$) that every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((\mathsf q))$ lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ lies in `R₀.integers` and has $R_0$-residue equal, as a Laurent series over the residue field of $A$, to the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$, $\ell'$ a prime, and $K_\ell$ an intermediate field of $k_0((\mathsf q))/k_0$ equal to the $k_0$-base change of the function field $\mathrm{xHFunctionField}$ of level $(q\ell')^2M'$ for $H$ the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/(q\ell')^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q\ell')^\times$, together with an algebra structure of $A\cap k_0$ on $K_\ell$ compatible with the tower, and a nonzero element $j_\ell\in K_\ell$ whose underlying Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion $j_{\mathsf q}$. Let $g\in\mathbb Q((\mathsf q))$ lie in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}\,M'$, assume its image in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ lies in `R₀.integers`, assume $g$ is regular wherever $j$ is, i.e. for every place $P$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ one has $P.\mathrm{ord}\,g\ge 0$ whenever $P.\mathrm{ord}\,j_{\mathsf q}\ge 0$, and assume that the substitution $\mathsf q\mapsto \mathsf q^{\ell'}$ applied to the coefficientwise image of $g$ over $k_0$ lies in $K_\ell$. Then that element of $K_\ell$ is integral over the $(A\cap k_0)$-subalgebra generated by $j_\ell$, i.e. it belongs to $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}$ for $A\cap k_0$, $K_\ell$ and $j_\ell$.
--
--   This is the integrality input for the finite ($j$-bounded) chart of the two-chart integral model of the modular curve at the auxiliary rigid level $(q\ell')^2M'$: a level-$M'$ modular function with $R_0$-integral $q$-expansion, regular where $j$ is regular, becomes integral over $(A\cap k_0)[j]$ after the substitution $\mathsf q\mapsto\mathsf q^{\ell'}$. It feeds the constructions of invariants and supersingular chart data at rigid level, such as [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.supersingularDVR_affineChart_invariants_of_rigidChart_framed`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.supersingularDVR_affineChart_invariants_of_rigidChart_framed).
